        contentType: 'TEXT',
        contentUrl: 'local-content',
        content: 'Responsible Service of Alcohol (RSA) is a mandatory national training framework regulated under state and territory liquor licensing legislation (e.g., Liquor Control Act 1988 in WA, Liquor Act 1992 in QLD). On FIFO sites, camps with licensed social clubs or bars must employ RSA-certified staff for all alcohol service. Study: the legal framework governing liquor service, duty of care obligations of licensees and staff, prohibited persons (under 18, intoxicated persons), and penalties for breaches — including personal fines, licence suspension, and criminal charges. Understand the concept of secondary supply and how it applies on site.',
